From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-microsoft-denali: keep CMA below 4 GiB

The default 128 MiB CMA pool has no allocation range. On the M8 boot it
lands at 0xbf8000000, outside the WCN7850's 32-bit coherent DMA mask.
The first QMI host-DDR allocation of 7274496 bytes consequently fails:
dma-direct rejects CMA pages above the mask, and this 4 KiB-page kernel
cannot satisfy an order-11 allocation from the buddy allocator (maximum
order 10). Firmware recovers by requesting smaller chunks, but the
initial allocation can be satisfied directly with reachable CMA memory.

Constrain the existing reusable pool to the lower RAM window, from
0x80000000 up to 4 GiB. Memblock still chooses its location around the
firmware reservations; no fixed address or larger pool is introduced.
The M8 EFI memory map contains multiple usable extents in this window
larger than 128 MiB. Keep the ath12k DMA masks and firmware protocol
intact.

Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
@@ -120,6 +120,7 @@
 		linux,cma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			size = <0x0 0x8000000>;
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x80000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
 			reusable;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
